  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 140 PM CST Wed Nov 11 2026\n\nA breezy and mild afternoon continues across the local area as\nan amplified area of high pressure across the intermountain \nwest extends north into the Canadian provinces and a trough of\nlow pressure extends south into the Great Lakes region. \nTonight, expect a backdoor cold front to our northeast to begin \nto slide south across the local area, bringing a return to below\nnormal temperatures for the next several days. Could see some \nincreased stratus with this front Thursday morning, along with \nsome patchy fog development just ahead of the front, but the \nbetter chance for any widespread dense fog development appears \nto be to our west where the HRRR is focusing this potential.\n\nCooler air will then settle in across the local area during the\nday Thursday, with afternoon temperatures struggling to reach 50\nacross the majority of our Nebraska coverage area, with some\nlower 50s possible across mainly north central Kansas Thursday\nafternoon. This will be noticably cooler than the past few \ndays, albeit very close to climatology which is in the lower 50s\nacross the majority of the local area. Continued cold air \nadvection will keep temperatures even cooler to end the week and\nthrough the upcoming weekend, with very few if any temperatures\ntopping out in the 50s anticipated. With clear skies and light \nwinds, Friday morning will be the coolest morning of the fall, \nthus far, with widespread low temperatures in the lower to \nmid-20s. \n\nLate in the weekend...expect an upper level disturbance to\nundercut the upper level ridge to our west and cross the \nsouthern plains Saturday night through Sunday. Despite cooler \nair being in place, this looks like a cold rain event as 850MB \ntemps will be 2-4C making the potential for any snow mixed in \nunlikely.\n\nModestly warmer temps will then build across the local area for\nthe first part of next week as heights aloft begin to rise as a\ntrough of low pressure digs across the west coast. This system\nwill then bring a chance of precip back to the entire area by\nthe middle of next week and looks to start a more active period\nof weather with multiple systems potentially bringing additional\nprecip chances just beyond the current 7 day forecast period.",
